This is my second ascension in the tournament (out of four games, not
to brag); I haven't done a knight since 3.2.2, when they were quite
different to today's spellcasting riding knights, so it seemed as good
a way as any to ascend a human character.

This knight began quite ordinarily, dipping for Excalibur ASAP,
finding the Mines and pressing down through them, robbing shops with
the aid of a leash - my original horse, Goto, was killed by the watch
captain, but I tamed a cat, Kanuka - until I inadvertently dragged her
across a polytrap, which turned her into a silver dragon. This seemed
like a good time to retrieve Goto's saddle.

Riding a flying pet has a lot to recommend it; however, even with
speed monster, dragons are quite slow (and don't forget to bring the
wand to Orcus so you can re-haste your dragons after they clean up the
shades); and later in the game my steeds were constantly being killed
from under me, and I hadn't realised the need to collect wands of
undead turning, so had only one with me. If I were going to do this
again I would probably wish for a figurine of a ki-rin, as a fast
self-healing self-hasting steed. I wore water walking boots in the
later game in case I was unhorsed (undragoned?) over water. Also a
carnivorous steed is like an insane corpse hoover, so you have to
gather and carry substantial quantities of food and do a dismounting
dance every time a useful monster heaves into view. Fortunately I
found a stethoscope very early on, so could monitor Kanuka's health.

It's become clear to me that a good player on a public server can
expect to reap enormous benefits from bones, and this game was no
exception. The first pile was from someone who had inexplicably died
to a minotaur on DL 5, the Oracle (why can't I get Sokoban this
shallow with characters like wizards who are desperate for it?);
Kanuka and I easily finished it off and took a small haul of Stuff -
including the victim monk's robe, which proved very useful.

I had already found enough gold to get naked AC 2 from the minetown
priest; I was then desperate for an altar (having several scrolls of
identify - I'd cleared out the minetown shops and shops on DL 2 and 4
by having Kanuka off the shopkeepers once I'd price-IDed identify) so
I let Kanuka off him and took my gold back; I would repeat this with
other priests (all of Brigit) on DL 8 and 13, getting a naked AC -1,
but was too lazy to drag my 100,000-odd gold down to the Valley.

After offing the priest on DL 8 I did a round of book blessing and got
ID at 56% failure in spellcasting rig, which was extremely useful. I
got the AoR Sokoban - handy since I'd got a BoH already.

I pressed quickly down to the Quest, reaching XL 14 with the help of a
wraith corpse. I would find a large number of PoGL in this game, and
as a spellcasting knight I wanted a high level anyway; I reached level
25 with around 350 mana, which didn't hurt. I did the Quest right
away; Ixoth blew up a pair of junk boots (I didn't wear any
irreplaceable armour to tackle him), but a potion of sickness and the
starting lance (the only time I used it) took care of him in short
order. Kanuka ate his corpse.

I got Ludious on DL 13 - convenient for donating to the priest there,
and for blanking/diluting in the moat once it was cleared; I shifted
my primary stash to this level quite soon after that. In this game I
made extensive use of controlled cursed/confused teleportation, which
made operations like this a lot less painful - this is something I
ought to have started doing years ago. I also got a set of black
dragon scales from Ludious, and made myself a BDSM to improve my AC
while looking for GDSM.

I pressed down towards Medusa; Kanuka ate a chameleon and became a
giant, but I was enjoying riding enough to recover back to the Mines
and bounce her into the polytrap until she turned into a orange
dragon.  I easily maxed Str with the many beehives I found - but the
first one contained a total of three bees, which I thought was taking
the piss a bit.

I was a little worried about not having found any useful special
armour items other than the robe - I had had no wishes from thrones,
and no magic lamps at all - so if the Castle wand was short on
charges, I could have had some difficult choices.

However, that all changed when I hit a maze on DL 26, above Medusa. Of
course this screams "bones pile", and a little exploration revealed
the grave of a player called "giblets" - and a minotaur, which Kanuka
and I disposed of in short order.

I have no idea what giblets was doing - scrolls and potions outside
the sack, fourteen lizard corpses (and a ton of other food), etc.
However, I wasn't complaining about the free GDSM, magic marker, and
other loot; and then on a hunch I explored a little more, to discover
the corpse of an unknown packrat wizard (sorry, I forgot the name)
killed by the same minotaur; Magicbane out for the taking, and a
cursed BoH - but giblets had left a WoCancel, and it was the work of a
moment to uncurse it to find Grayswandir (and Dragonbane, meh) in the
bag, along with a vast heap of loot including a good many spellbooks -
charm monster probably the most useful. I am not a packrat, of
course, but I certainly appreciate it when other people are!

I would also find a bones pile on DL 28 from a "viljami", but it paled
into insignificance next to the DL 26 find, which I think is the
single largest bones haul I have ever made. Some of the magic markers
were exhausted, but I still wasn't complaining...

Medusa and the Castle were no problem; I tamed two more silver dragons
at the Castle, Izumi and Shinobu. The real limiting factor here was
not realising it was worth collecting wands of speed monster, not a
shortage of dragons. The Castle wand had only one charge, but I didn't
need so much equipment anymore; GoDex, a HoBrilliance, and a ring of
free action; I burned the remaining two on a spellbook of finger of
death (and then remembered I wanted cure sickness, but I wrote that
first time with a marker, luckily) and two charging scrolls to
maximise the use of my markers.

I got a pet vampire, Cassidy, from a magic trap on the Valley;
unfortunately I lost Kanuka at Asmodeus (one of the other dragons ate
her corpse), and I was starting to have to undead-turn Shinobu and
Izumi if I didn't pay close attention to their hitpoints. One of them
was slimed at Orcus, but with a polytrap on the level I quickly turned
her into a white dragon. At Vlad's I then tamed a grey dragon,
Shinohara, as another spare steed.

With this horde of pets I quickly got to the vibrating square and
cleaned out the first two levels of Rodney's tower; then levelported
back to the stash and dropped off the DL 1 care package. I didn't have
the same worries about holy water, since after Rodney was dead I could
run around with Magicbane when not fighting - it blasted me
periodically, but after a big alchemy session I had about 380 HP, so
who cared?

I did not take the pets into the Sanctum save for Izumi, who I was
riding, and who was (alas) killed in the Sanctum unrecoverably; I made
the stylish cursed PoGL exit. Of course the horde of pets does not
work at all on the way back up; you can't traverse the stairs
repeatedly because of the mysterious force, so you're left magic
whistling turn after turn until they're all next to you. I ditched the
rest and rode Shinobu, but was finally unhorsed around DL 44 - the
dragons' slow speed was becoming more of a liability here. The right
thing to do would have been to have left them all at the Valley by
levelporting back immediately before doing the incantation, and
periodically drop the Amulet and levelport back to them to keep them
tame - more generally, the fact that one can drop the Amulet and
levelport out of Gehennom isn't something one sees exploited much.

The mysterious force was sheer hell below Orcus; if I hadn't had
Magicbane my anti-curse resources would be been severely strained. I
did, however, find a magic lamp just as my final light source was used
up - lucky, eh? As it was I quickly used up my wands of death and was
reduced to giving Rodney the Finger when he showed up - I had an 18%
failure chance, but he never did anything annoying on the occasions I
didn't get it off first time. Once I finally cleared Orcus (after
about five trips across it) things eased up, and I quickly exited
Gehennom.

Earth was easy; Air burned one PoFH, but didn't provide any serious
worry; Fire and Water were both straightforward enough - surplus SoGD
helped locate the portal on Water.

On the Astral Plane I made extensive use of charm monster, but forgot
the 3 scrolls of taming I had brought to use confused taming with.
First I managed to outmaneuver Death en route to the left altar,
taking one round of attacks and then breaking off the action, but that
wasn't right; I dodged Death completely on the way out. Pestilence had
the central altar and came out of his door; however, the Finger took
care of that, and I whistled in my horde of ants to block a further
exodus out that area while I tackled Famine. Famine attacked me
several times, but since I had taken the precaution of satiating
myself and carrying planty of K-rats, he was no trouble; I managed to
beat on him just enough to make him flee, and his altar proved to be
the right one - and for the first time ever I managed to ascend with
the guardian Angel still alive and next to me.

70,000 moves is medium long, but 2,702 creatures vanquished is
relatively low for me. As well as the recorded polypiling and artifact
wishing conducts, I spurned Elbereth and conflict, and was not
lifesaved - in fact in this game I never wore an AoLS. My equipment
and highlights of the kill list are below.

